WEBVTT

00:00:06.798 --> 00:00:08.091
Pity about that

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.550
chocolate fella Wendell.

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:10.635
Uh, Walter.

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:11.677
Willy Wonka.

00:00:11.761 --> 00:00:12.929
That’s the one.

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:14.222
Says here in the papers

00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:16.641
his new candies
aren’t selling very well.

00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:18.434
But I suppose maybe
he’s just

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:20.645
a rotten egg
who deserves it.

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:21.646
Yep.

00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:23.189
Oh, really?

00:00:23.231 --> 00:00:25.358
You ever met him?

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.360
I did.

00:00:27.401 --> 00:00:29.612
I thought he was great,
at first,

00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:32.031
but then,
he didn’t turn out so nice.

00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:34.951
He also has a funny haircut.

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:37.161
I do not.

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.955
Why are you here?

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:40.373
I don’t feel so hot.

00:00:40.456 --> 00:00:44.001
What makes you feel better
when you feel terrible?

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:45.378
My family.

00:00:45.461 --> 00:00:47.505
Ew.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.050
What do you have
against my family?

00:00:51.134 --> 00:00:54.846
It’s not just your family,
it’s the whole idea of...

00:00:56.889 --> 00:00:58.558
( groans )

00:00:58.599 --> 00:01:01.269
You know, they’re always telling
you what to do, what not to do,

00:01:01.352 --> 00:01:03.271
and it’s not conducive
to a creative atmosphere.

00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:05.398
Usually they’re just
trying to protect you,

00:01:05.481 --> 00:01:06.899
because they love you.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.404
If you don’t
believe me, you should ask.

00:01:11.445 --> 00:01:14.407
Ask who, my father?

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:15.616
( mocking chuckle )

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.785
No way.

00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:20.371
At least not by myself.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.748
You want me to go with you?

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:27.170
Hey... hey,
what a good idea.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.297
Yeah.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.091
And you know what?

00:01:32.175 --> 00:01:33.259
I’ve got transpor...

00:01:33.301 --> 00:01:35.511
( thud )

00:01:38.055 --> 00:01:40.391
I have to be more careful
where I park this thing.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.226
( bell dings )

00:01:44.061 --> 00:01:45.062
( bell dings )

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:47.106
( whirring )

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:50.234
( whooshing )

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:58.409
( whirring )

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:09.754
( light, mysterious music
playing )

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.841
I think we’ve
got the wrong house.

00:02:17.386 --> 00:02:18.971
( doorbell buzzes )

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.684
( door creaking )

00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:30.316
Do you have an appointment?

00:02:30.399 --> 00:02:33.236
No, but he’s overdue.

00:02:35.947 --> 00:02:37.323
Open.

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:40.326
Now,

00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:43.579
let’s see what
the damage is, shall we?

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:59.929
( quiet, gentle melody plays )

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.690
♪ ♪

00:03:20.866 --> 00:03:23.035
♪ ♪

00:03:23.077 --> 00:03:25.871
Heavens.

00:03:25.955 --> 00:03:29.667
I haven’t seen bicuspids
like these since...

00:03:32.128 --> 00:03:35.631
...since...

00:03:44.098 --> 00:03:46.017
Willy?

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:49.478
Hi, Dad.

00:03:59.322 --> 00:04:02.408
All these years,

00:04:02.491 --> 00:04:05.745
and you haven’t flossed.

00:04:05.786 --> 00:04:08.873
Not once.

00:04:18.632 --> 00:04:22.762
( simple, gentle melody playing
)

00:04:32.938 --> 00:04:34.940
NARRATOR:
It was on this day

00:04:34.982 --> 00:04:38.277
that Willy Wonka repeated
his offer to Charlie,

00:04:38.319 --> 00:04:40.321
who accepted
on one condition...

00:04:40.404 --> 00:04:42.365
Sorry we’re late.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.200
We were brainstorming.

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:45.785
Thought I heard
thunder.

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.536
Can you stay for dinner, Willy?

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.122
Oh, yes, please.

00:04:50.206 --> 00:04:52.792
I’ll shuffle
the plates.

00:04:58.506 --> 00:05:00.049
( chair creaks )

00:05:00.132 --> 00:05:03.469
You smell like
peanuts.

00:05:04.887 --> 00:05:06.847
I love peanuts.

00:05:06.931 --> 00:05:07.890
Oh, thank you.

00:05:07.973 --> 00:05:12.395
You smell like...
old people and soap.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.606
I like it.

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:16.982
( squeals happily )

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:22.571
Elbows off
the table, Charlie.

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.825
How do you feel about
little raspberry kites?

00:05:25.866 --> 00:05:28.119
With licorice instead of string.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:29.829
Boys...

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:31.330
no business at the dinner table.

00:05:31.372 --> 00:05:32.665
Sorry, Mum.

00:05:32.748 --> 00:05:36.544
I think you’re onto something,
though, Charlie.

